  "notes": [
    "The panel is a raw dot-clock display without a controller or frame memory: the host refreshes it continuously (about 60 Hz at a 9-15 MHz pixel clock) from a frame buffer.",
    "With 16 colour lines (RGB565) tie R0-R2, G0-G1 and B0-B2 to ground.",
    "The white LED backlight (12 LEDs) needs a constant-current boost to about 25.6 V at 40 mA: MT3608 with a 15 ohm sense resistor on FB (0.6 V).",
    "DISP high (or open on this panel: default on) shows the image; low is standby."
  ],
